<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Butler dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Butler</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Butler dynasty was an Anglo-Norman family in Ireland descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theobald-walter">Theobald Walter</a>, who held the hereditary office of butler of Ireland from 1185. As earls, later marquesses and dukes, of Ormond they dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> and Tipperary and were the great rivals of the FitzGeralds. They owned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny-castle">Kilkenny Castle</a> from 1391 until 1967.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/butler-dynasty.jpg" alt="Butler dynasty" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikimandia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Butler_arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
